// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.block [Ref-Binding-Last-Use] (the deferred end, D-0221, CHG-0260); conf.ref-holding-binding-end-deferred
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
// stdout: 2
//
// `h1` copies `r1`'s path. `h1` is last mentioned in its own declaration,
// but it shares that statement with `r1`, which is mentioned after it, so
// its end waits until `r1` is no longer mentioned: both end after
// `*r1 = *r1 + 1`, and reading `y` meets no live exclusive path. The text
// before D-0221 held `h1` to its block's exit, and the read faulted; both
// implementations always deferred (D-0219 finding 8).

import std;

struct Hold
{
    ref<i32, exclusive> r;
}

fn main()
{
    i32 y = 1;
    auto r1 = &mut y;
    Hold h1 = Hold { .r = r1 };
    *r1 = *r1 + 1;
    printf("%v\n", y);
}
